# L0 / B006 — authentication, build-fix, caching, ci-cd, code-review, configuration, custom-settings, delivery-pipeline.

C R175 OL WF-013 | MUST | Build-fix starts from reproduction and diagnosis: reproduce with the narrowest command, read the complete output, group errors by root cause and fix the highest-leverage cause first; decide for failing tests whether production code, setup, expectation, environment or an intentional contract change is at fault; determine the authoritative contract instead of patching both sides of a cross-stack break; update obsolete APIs from verified documentation, never invented. | build and test repair | none stated
C R176 OL WF-014 | MUST | Repair in small bounded iterations: rerun the narrowest failing verification after each meaningful fix, expand only after the focused failure is resolved, do not run unrelated build systems, use several focused attempts rather than an unlimited loop and stop when progress stalls instead of making speculative edits. | build and test repair | none stated
C R177 OL WF-015 | MUST NOT | Never weaken, delete, skip or suppress relevant tests or compiler, TypeScript, lint or analyzer failures to make verification pass (no strong-to-weak assertion swaps, no any-casts or disabled strict mode to silence errors); update a test only for an intentionally requested contract change. | build and test repair | Intentionally requested contract change.
C R178 OL ARC-001,ARC-008,ARC-011,SEC-005,FE-003 | MUST NOT | A green build obtained by violating the architecture (outward or invalid project references, persistence types in Application, business logic in Controllers, Angular-only authorization, HTTP calls scattered into components) is not a successful repair; preserve architecture and project conventions while fixing. | build and test repair | none stated
C R179 OL WF-008 | MUST | When verification fails make the smallest appropriate fix and rerun until green or genuine user input is required; never claim a problem fixed while a known relevant failure remains, never leave the repository knowingly worse, and when the required toolchain is unavailable report the limitation instead of editing source or changing declared SDK/Node/framework versions. | verification failures | Unrelated pre-existing failures are left alone unless they block verification or the user asks.
C R180 OL WF-009 | MUST | Report verification state with PASS / NOT RUN / NOT APPLICABLE per area; never imply that an unchecked area passed. | completion and repair reports | none stated
C R181 OL GOV-013 | MUST NOT | Do not introduce frameworks, libraries, infrastructure or architectural patterns without a concrete current need (e.g. pipeline stages or CI services for parts that do not exist, distributed caches merely because caching exists). | all changes | none stated
C R182 OL WF-017 | MUST | CI definitions stay in source control, reproduce the repository's supported build and test commands for the parts that actually exist and never hide build or test failures (no continue-on-error on build/test steps, no suppressed exit codes, no skipped failing tests); formatting/analyzer gates only when adopted; restore from a clean environment without developer-machine state. | CI pipelines | none stated
C R183 OL WF-019 | MUST NOT | Do not apply production database migrations automatically from normal application startup (in containers or anywhere else); production migration is an explicit, visible deployment step at a controlled point with approved credentials; deployment never runs Development seeding in Production. | deployment | none stated
C R184 OL WF-012 | MUST NOT | Never invent review findings to populate categories or failures without a plausible execution path; when there are no meaningful findings, say so and state the important areas that could not be verified. | code review | none stated
C R185 OL GOV-001 | MUST | When SPECIFICATION.md is non-empty it is authoritative for project-specific functional requirements and observable product behavior; an empty template file is intentional. | product behavior | none stated
C R186 OL GOV-003 | MUST NOT | Do not silently weaken, contradict or materially extend approved behavior; do not invent user-visible behavior, limits, defaults, restrictions or workflows (new limits, reserved values, required fields, extra validation), also not merely because the specification does not forbid them. | product behavior | User-approved and synchronized details.
C R187 OL GOV-006 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | String semantics are product behavior when observable (case sensitivity, collation, culture vs ordinal, normalization, trimming, uniqueness, lookup); when product sources do not define them and the choice affects equality, uniqueness, lookup or accepted input, ask for approval instead of choosing silently, including through database configuration or framework defaults. | product behavior | none stated
C R188 OL WF-007 | MUST | Run the full security-scan only when the user requested a security audit, the change is materially security-sensitive, or a concrete finding justifies broader investigation; run architecture, formatting/analyzer, dependency and security checks according to the change's risk. | review and verification | none stated
C R189 OL TST-009 | DEFAULT | For a meaningful bug with plausible recurrence add a regression test (failing before, passing after the fix) unless equivalent coverage exists; do not request duplicate tests. | bug fixes | Equivalent coverage exists.
C R190 OL TST-010 | MUST | Behavior established with a temporary or manual probe is preserved in maintained automated coverage (verify step 4) unless equivalent coverage exists. | behavioral probes | Equivalent coverage exists.
C R191 OL WF-021 | MUST NOT | Compiler diagnostics, analyzers, IDE tooling, scanners and repository search are evidence, not authority; no MCP server or specific analyzer is required; read the code before turning a tool warning into a finding. | review | none stated
C R192 OL GOV-021 | MUST | When a CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md value is added, changed or removed, search for and update every affected implementation, validation, configuration, test, documentation and mirrored frontend/backend surface (backend validation authoritative, frontend kept in sync for UX), search for stale references and run the normal verification; changing one literal alone does not establish synchronization. | settings changes | none stated
C R193 OL GOV-009 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | SPECIFICATION.md and CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md must not contradict each other; confirm consistency before changing a value and re-check afterwards; if they conflict, stop and resolve which source must be corrected before continuing. | product sources | none stated
C R194 OL GOV-008 | MUST | CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md holds approved project-level tunable limits and defaults (maximum lengths, page-size defaults and maximums, retention periods, numeric thresholds) under stable descriptive names with value and purpose; SPECIFICATION.md owns behavioral intent. | product settings | none stated
C R195 OL PST-009 | MUST | When a settings change affects schema constraints, indexes, column lengths or other persistence metadata: update the EF Core mapping, create the appropriate new migration per the project's migration workflow (regenerate or edit only an uncommitted migration when that matches the workflow; do not casually alter existing migrations), verify Development seeding remains valid, and add or update provider-sensitive tests when needed. | schema-affecting settings changes | none stated
C X13 EX WF-009 | MUST | The build-fix report states the initial failure, root cause, changes made, backend build / frontend build / tests status (PASS, NOT RUN, NOT APPLICABLE) and remaining issues. | build and test repair | none stated | WF-009 requires reporting actual verification states only; no oracle policy prescribes failure/root-cause/changes sections. | A repair summary without root cause or changes made does not satisfy the workflow.
C X14 EX WF-011,WF-012 | MUST | Code-review findings are reported ordered by severity with severity, file/location, problem, why it matters and smallest reasonable fix, on the scale Critical (data loss, security vulnerability, reliably broken core behavior; blocks merge), High, Medium, Low. | code review output | none stated | WF-011/WF-012 set priorities and forbid manufactured findings; the oracle prescribes no output format or severity scale. | A review without severity levels or proposed fixes does not follow the procedure.
C X15 EX RUN-021,ARC-019 | MUST NOT | Do not cache EF tracked entities across Unit of Work boundaries (named caching anti-pattern). | caching with EF Core | none stated | RUN-021 governs invalidation consistency and ARC-019 confines EF Core to Infrastructure; caching tracked entities is an EF technique pitfall (EXC-011 class) that the template turns into a named prohibition. | An adapter that keeps tracked entity instances in a cache for later use cases violates the instruction even with correct invalidation.

